# Copy to .env.local. Every value here is public: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into
# the browser bundle at build time.
#
# ── Hosted (Vercel; docs/deploy.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# A public deployment sets these in the project's Environment Variables, then
# builds (a change needs a redeploy, since they are compiled in):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POLARIS_API_URL=https://<Polaris for Business>   required
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=10143                                   Monad testnet
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_RP_ID=<the app's domain, or a domain it is under> strongly advised
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=<the dashboard's Privy app>          optional (email)
# and never NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER, NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER_PERSIST,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCAL_DEMO or NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCAL_FAUCET_URL. GET /api/health
# reports what the build has; scripts/deploy-check.mjs checks it.

# The WebAuthn relying party. A passkey, and so a Polaris account, is tied to
# it forever. Production: polarispay.app (serves app. and pay.). Leave it unset
# in dev to use the page's hostname (localhost).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RP_ID=polarispay.app

# Dev only. "1" replaces Face ID with a random key kept in this tab's
# sessionStorage, so flows can be exercised headlessly. A "Dev signer" badge
# shows whenever it is on. Never set it in a deployed environment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER=1

# Polaris for Business: the relayer (POST /api/relay), checkout sessions
# (/api/public/sessions/{id}) and the network's contracts and EIP-712 domains.
# Local: http://localhost:3100. Required: unset, every route shows "Polaris
# isn't configured on this build", with no data, and nothing can be signed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POLARIS_API_URL=http://localhost:3100

# Chain. 10143 is Monad testnet, 143 is Monad mainnet.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=10143
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXPLORER_URL=https://testnet.monadvision.com

# Verifying contracts. They come from NEXT_PUBLIC_POLARIS_API_URL's
# /api/public/network (the deployment record), with their EIP-712 domains; set
# here, they pin this build and the app refuses to sign if the server reports
# different ones. Unset NEXT_PUBLIC_AUSD_ADDRESS means the server's dollar.
# The Monad testnet deployment (packages/contracts/deployments/monad-testnet.json,
# 28 Sep 2026). Its dollar is MockAUSD: a mock dollar for the testnet demo,
# clearly labelled ("Mock AUSD"), which anyone can mint. It is not Agora's AUSD,
# because the deployer held no testnet AUSD to seed the credit pool with.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUSD_ADDRESS=0x3F9554F15f58Bb5900822224f37A05be81eF9723
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYMENTS_ADDRESS=0x7C774CF3E664B10057Cb2dDa66bA298e831292F1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHECKOUT_ADDRESS=0x3874ef1bcE222755525a96f8284631780b9bC70B
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SEND_ADDRESS=0x67D336c69881A4f3Fa4aaa2909cfcD95178DfC55
# PolarisSplit (split-the-bill links) is not on Monad testnet yet:
# `pnpm --filter @polarispay/contracts deploy-split:monad` adds it to this
# deployment. Until then Split a bill says it isn't available here. After it,
# leave this unset (the API reports it) or pin it:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SPLIT_ADDRESS=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOAN_ENGINE_ADDRESS=0xDaf74fa6A5cF2e03DF8E12613a8c8BF3A569204a

# Privy: "Continue with email" beneath Face ID. The same Privy app as the
# dashboard. Unset hides the option. Google is off in the Privy app.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
# Optional: a Privy app client for the web origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_CLIENT_ID=
# ── pnpm demo:local only (`next dev`) ────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/demo-local.mjs sets these; `next build` blanks the dev signer ones.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER=1 stands a key in browser storage in for Face ID;
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER_PERSIST=1 keeps it for the device (localStorage), so a
# shop's checkout popup opens as the same buyer as the app's tab.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SIGNER_PERSIST=
# The local faucet the Add money sheet offers on chain 31337 (POST {address}).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCAL_FAUCET_URL=
# 1 on a local chain: "Raise your limit" may use a stand-in history wallet.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCAL_DEMO=

# A native Android build only: NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_TARGET=android makes the bundle
# use NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID (an app client locked to the Android
# package). The web build never passes it as its clientId. The Android app in
# apps/android is a Trusted Web Activity that opens the hosted web build, so it
# needs neither.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_TARGET=android
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=

# Server only (not NEXT_PUBLIC), read per request: Digital Asset Links for the
# Android app (apps/android), served at /.well-known/assetlinks.json. The
# SHA-256 fingerprints of every certificate the app is signed with (the local
# or upload key, and Play's app signing key), comma-separated;
# `pnpm --filter @polaris/android fingerprint` prints the local one. Unset: the
# route is 404, and the Android app opens with an address bar.
# POLARIS_ANDROID_SHA256_FINGERPRINTS=
# POLARIS_ANDROID_PACKAGE=app.polarispay.twa

# Server only (not NEXT_PUBLIC): where /api/fx reads the Chainlink FX feeds for
# the local-currency line. Comma-separated JSON-RPC URLs; the defaults are
# public, keyless endpoints (packages/fx/src/feeds.ts). Read-only calls.
# FX_RPC_MONAD=https://rpc.monad.xyz,https://rpc1.monad.xyz
# FX_RPC_ETHEREUM=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com,https://cloudflare-eth.com
# FX_RPC_POLYGON=https://polygon-bor-rpc.publicnode.com,https://1rpc.io/matic
# FX_RPC_BASE=https://mainnet.base.org,https://base-rpc.publicnode.com
